any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# buys our #paper# and sends back #rags# with smoke in them. | I prefer the air over our #field#.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : A loud crowd and spilled drink leave me looking for a dry #floor#. | I can hear the #music# from #home#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I have carried #stacks# for grand houses without ever seeing who uses the #sheets#. | The #hands# still do the lifting.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : My #wages# will not buy the #bread# I need for a #shift#. | A #buyer# can call that a small difference.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Let a new #hand# learn the #vat# before taking someone's #shift#. | The #work# has an order.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# takes finished #paper# to the #market#. | It sends muddy #wagons# across our #floor#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : I count more #coins# for the same #loaf# every season. | The #pulp# has not become easier to lift.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The watch can keep the #gate# clear. | I will mind the #mill# #door# myself.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Keep your feet clear of the #vat#. | #greet#. The #sheets# are drying.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come in; the #soup# is still warm. | I swept the #floor# before you arrived.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The first #stack# is already on the #board#. | #greet#. The #vat# is full this #morning#.
line @1 greet.return : You returned before this #sheet# dried. | The #planks# are clear now.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There is a #bowl# at our #table#. | Mind the wet #boots# at the #door#.
line @1 again.open : I was checking the #deckle# #edge#. | Did the #wagon# reach the #market#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must lift the next #sheet#. | Step around the #drain#.
line @1 farewell.return : The finished #paper# will be here on your return. | The #soup# may still be warm.
line @1 react.news : Say it while I empty this #mould#. | Was it by the #gate#?
line @1 react.news.new : No word of that reached our #mill#. | Did a #wagon# bring it?
line @1 react.news.known : A #seller# mentioned a small part. | Your account fills the gap.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would see the #sheet# before judging the #edge#. | Which witness saw the whole matter clearly?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Take the #bowl#; I will finish this #stack#. | I am sorry. We can sit when the #press# stops.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That merits a fresh #bowl# for supper. | I will mark a clean #sheet# for them.
line @1 answer.how : The #vat# stayed clear and the #house# is tidy. | I saw the #stars# after a warm #rain#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : This #pulp# must settle before I leave. | The #press# needs another #stack#.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# leave your #boots# dry? | Have you eaten more than stale #bread#?
line @1 sympathise : I can set this #mould# down and listen. | A warm #bowl# may make the #hour# easier.
line @1 reassure : A torn #sheet# can be put back in the #vat#. | The wet #floor# is drying now.
line @1 decline : No, I will not put that #paper# through the #press# yet. | I have to clear the #drain# first.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we will leave the #stack# for tomorrow. | I hear you; the #vat# can wait.
line @1 thank : You moved the #bucket# out of the walkway. | The fresh #bread# was a kind thought.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #broom# was already in my #hand#. | I had an extra #bowl#.
line @1 preclose : The #sky# is darkening over the #mill#. | One last sweep will leave the #floor# safe.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : That #vat# would hide a #sheet# from you. | Your #march# has fewer beats than a broken #press#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #edge# is straight. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will take the next #stack#.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the #deckle# level when lifting #paper#. | Dry the #planks# before carrying a full #bucket#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Travel with the #wagon# on the #road#. | I would wait until the #gate# is busy.
scene clean_vat
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dirty #water# leaves specks in every #sheet#. | I rinse the #vat# before adding fresh #pulp#.
b : Does that take long? | Can you remove the specks?
a : Less than remaking a #stack#. | Only while the #paper# is wet.

scene deckle_edge
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I hold the #deckle# level so the #pulp# settles evenly. | A tilted lift makes one #edge# too thin.
b : Can you see it at once? | Do you lift again?
a : While the #sheet# shines. | If it has not set.

scene marching_lift
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The old #march# comes to me as I lift #sheets# from the #vat#. | The #beat# keeps my #hands# steady.
b : Does anyone join in? | Why that tune?
a : When the #mill# is quiet. | It is easy to remember.

scene press_stack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stack# under the #press# needs flat #boards# above and below. | A curled #plank# leaves a mark through the middle.
b : Do you replace the board? | Is the paper lost?
a : Before pressing. | It can return to the #vat#.

scene dry_board
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I spread each #sheet# on a dry #board# after the #press#. | If the edges touch, they cling together.
b : How long do they dry? | Do you turn them?
a : Until the #wind# has passed over. | Once, with clean #hands#.

scene floor_drain
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I clear the #drain# before the #floor# grows slick. | A #bucket# in the wrong place can trip a carrying #hand#.
b : Has someone fallen? | Who cleans it?
a : Not on my #shift#. | When the #drain# looks slow.

scene barley_soup
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Barley #soup# needs enough time by the #fire# to thicken. | Whoever closes the #mill# gets a full #bowl#.
b : Do you cook it? | Is there bread?
a : When the #house# is quiet. | Fresh if I can get it.

scene stale_loaf
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A stale #loaf# takes more chewing than a hard #shift#. | I soften it in #soup# rather than waste it.
b : Does it taste better? | Is there another way?
a : With enough #barley#. | A warm #fire# helps.

scene tidy_house
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set the #bucket# and #broom# by the #door# when I come #home#. | A tidy #floor# lets me stop thinking of the #mill#.
b : Do you clean every evening? | Does anyone help?
a : The mud, at least. | When I ask.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A warm #rain# after a dry #day# settles the dust outside the #mill#. | I still keep the #paper# away from the #window#.
b : Do you like walking in it? | Does the paper curl?
a : After the #shift#. | If the #wind# drives it inside.

scene evening_stars
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I look for the first #star# after the #press# stops. | The #sky# is cleaner than the #vat# on a hard #day#.
b : Do you know its name? | Do you stay outside?
a : Only the one I always find. | Until the #house# calls.

scene wet_planks
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Wet #planks# near the #press# hold water long after the #rain# ends. | I walk the dry #edge# with a #stack#.
b : Does the wood rot? | Is there another path?
a : If nobody tends it. | Along the wall.

scene paper_buyer
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #buyer# can see a crooked #edge# before I say a word. | I would rather offer the clean #sheets# and state the #price#.
b : Do buyers mind rough paper? | Do you set the price?
a : Some use it for drafts. | I tell the #seller# what is sound.

scene city_rags
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #wagon# from the #city# brought #rags# dark with #smoke#. | We washed them twice before they reached the #vat#.
b : Did they make paper? | Was it worth the work?
a : After the second rinse. | The #mill# needed them.

scene shared_cottage
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# gathers paper and #linen# #hands# around one #table#. | I sweep before the late #shift# comes in.
b : Is there room? | Does everyone eat together?
a : If we move the #buckets#. | When the hours meet.

scene old_road_walk
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I walked the #road# to the #city# once and came home with sore feet. | The #stars# over our #field# looked better on my return.
b : Was the city useful? | Would you go again?
a : I learned how large a #market# can be. | Only for work.

scene festival_noise
when topic=home here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Festival #music# reaches the #mill# through the #window#. | I finish a #stack# before deciding whether to go out.
b : Do you join them? | Is it loud?
a : For a short #hour#. | Loud enough to hear indoors.

story first_clean_sheet [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : My first #sheet# came from the #vat# with a ragged #edge#.
  : I tried again with the #deckle# level and a slower lift.
  ask : Was the second better?
  b : A patient hand.
  : Straight enough for the #press#.

story spilled_bucket [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : While I carried a #stack#, someone knocked a #bucket# over by the #press#.
  : I set the #paper# down and cleared the #floor# before lifting it again.
  ask : Was any paper ruined?
  b : You chose your footing.
  : Only the bottom #sheet# went back to the #vat#.

story city_journey [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : I walked to the #city# once to see where our #paper# went.
  : The #market# was crowded, and the #road# home seemed longer in the dark.
  b : A long day. Would you return?
  : For a reason, not for the crowd.

rule @bark_vat
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #vat# needs clean #water#. | Lift that #sheet# level.

rule @bark_press
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Mind the #press# #plank#. | This #stack# belongs on dry #boards#.

rule @bark_floor
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Clear the #drain# before carrying #paper#. | That #bucket# blocks the path.

rule @bark_star
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The first #star# is out. | I will finish this #stack# before supper.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #vat# is ready for another #sheet#. | #greet#. Mind the wet #floor#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You came back while the #paper# dried. | I remember you; the #deckle# is level now.
dlg @1 resident.job : I lift #paper# from the #vat# at #self.workplace#. | The #mould#, #press#, and dry #boards# keep me busy.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I have to clear the #drain#. | #saying.capitalize#. Keep your #boots# dry.
graft resident.hub
choice How is paper made here? -> paper
node paper
say We soak #rags# into #pulp#, lift it on a #mould#, and dry each #sheet# after the #press#.
free
choice Why hum that tune? -> tune
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node tune
say The #march# keeps my #hands# steady when I lift a wet #sheet# from the #vat#.
choice Back to the vat. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #vat# has settled. | #greet#. The #press# is clear.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will stack the last #sheets#. | The #stars# should be out by then.
